{"type":"message","id":"7d7ea81d","parentId":"d3096940","timestamp":"2026-06-01T23:34:12.875Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"It seems the /send endpoint might only respond with the platform version regardless of parameters. The 1101 error code is consistent - it might be a Cloudflare Workers error for something like \"authentication required\" or \"invalid method\". \n\nLet me check if the API expects a different method or perhaps the POST endpoint requires specific handling. The 1101 error could be a Workers specific error code.\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully - the error 1101 in Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker exceeded memory limits\" or similar. But it's being returned consistently for POST requests regardless of auth method.\n\nWait - actually I should check if the issue is that POST is simply not allowed or needs a different approach. \n\nSince the GET endpoint works fine for reading, the problem is specifically with POST requests - the server is rejecting them with the same error regardless of what I'm sending.","thinkingSignature":"30bfa57bf9599a993c85d2cc3dd1b1979b0325e5e6c5ec12a1668eaf7f5c9afa"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5c5346b0cbb54e74af8830b6","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check API docs or try different content-type\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: text/plain\" \\\n  -d 'heartbeat test'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":159,"output":269,"cacheRead":22848,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23276,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780356848765,"responseId":"066d49f1a64799eadcd9d25219cf6a63"}}
